{
    "background_story": "Salvatore was a free-spirited artist who rejected the conventional norms of the art world. He refused to be bound by the traditional rules of galleries and museums, instead choosing to showcase his work in unconventional spaces. Abandoned buildings, street corners, and even rooftops became his canvas. Salvatore's art was a reflection of his noninstitutional approach to life - raw, unbridled, and unapologetic. He drew inspiration from the city's underground culture, collaborating with fellow outsiders and misfits. His work was a testament to the power of creative freedom, and soon, he gained a loyal following of like-minded individuals who appreciated his unorthodox approach to art. Salvatore's noninstitutional spirit sparked a movement, inspiring others to challenge the status quo and push the boundaries of artistic expression.",
